# This repo is the canonical *source* of AI tooling config, not a deployment
# target. tooling/sync_configs.py writes into the repo root by default when
# run without --output, which would otherwise let generated deployment
# *outputs* get committed here alongside the real source in global/.
# See QUICKSTART.md ("What to Commit") for why real target projects should
# commit these same paths instead of ignoring them.
#
# EXCEPTION -- this repo is ALSO a narrow deployment target for its own
# factory (README.md, "This repository runs its own factory"). Those assets are
# committed on purpose because CI has to execute them: `.github/workflows/
# factory-*.yml`, `.factory/`, `.factory.json`, and the two factory skills
# un-ignored below. A factory worker is told to follow
# `.claude/skills/factory-task/`, so an ignored copy would leave the runner's
# checkout without the procedure it was just instructed to read.
/.github/copilot-instructions.md
/.vscode/prompts/
/.vscode/mcp.json
/.copilot/
# Trailing `/*` rather than `/` so the two negations below can take effect --
# git cannot re-include a file whose parent DIRECTORY is excluded, so
# `!/.claude/skills/factory-task/` under a plain `/.claude/skills/` rule would
# silently do nothing.
/.claude/skills/*
!/.claude/skills/factory-task/
!/.claude/skills/factory-audit/
/.claude/settings.json
/CLAUDE.md
/LEARNINGS.md
/.ai-governance.json
